<h2>Experience</h2>

<h3>Head of Experience Design, Totara Learning</h3>
<p class="label label--meta">January 2022 to present · Wellington</p>
<p>Leads design across Totara's learning platform, covering UX strategy, design systems, accessibility and design-to-code tooling. Leads a team of designers and researchers, and the move to an AI-first design practice.</p>
<ul>
	<li>Initiated and led Inspire, a cross-team R&amp;D programme that shipped in Totara 19: a new default theme with side navigation, a task-based information architecture, a rebuilt catalogue, a single library and workspace overview, and correct page headings across the product. Wrote the business case, consulted 12 strategic partners, and steered platform, product, QA and documentation teams through three delivery increments.</li>
	<li>Shaped a layered design token architecture that lets the legacy LMS and the new multi-product app framework share one design system, with a build check that turns token gaps into build failures.</li>
	<li>Led an accessibility and dark-mode audit that produced a prioritised remediation register, including a focus-ring change across 21 components that raised contrast from about 2:1 to almost 5:1.</li>
	<li>Wrote a product health model that divides the platform into 25 owned capability areas, scores health and strategic importance separately, and runs a monthly AI-assisted review of customer demand and NPS.</li>
	<li>Restructured six years of scattered research notes into a directory that product managers now maintain: 408 entries since 2022, 97% of them added by 16 colleagues across product and R&amp;D.</li>
	<li>Moved the team to an AI-first practice that uses AI to measure design quality, including a tool that maps all 471 legacy global variables to the new token contract.</li>
</ul>

